    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d862">

                <pb facs="0859" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5012 b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commissioner at
                        Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-13T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1919—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>You may take any practicable means to convey informally to the Esthonian
                    authorities the suggestion that accession on their part to the reported
                    Bolshevik proposal of free transit through Esthonian territory and use of
                    Esthonian ports would tend to place Esthonia in a position of subserviency to
                    Soviet Russia which might make it worse than dependent. Having regard to
                    Esthonia’s slight territorial extent and feeble economy, it is not to be
                    supposed that if such an arrangement were once established Esthonia would be
                    able successfully to resist an inevitable tendency to encroach further upon its
                    sovereignty. The proposal opens the way in fact for a practical nullification of
                    the independence which the Bolsheviki pretend to be willing to grant to
                    Esthonia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
